From 8f07bb95d5866af4cd81133f36e61d0ed7af2093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:14:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Fix incident persistence, ID reuse, scoring, correlation
 and scenario targeting

- PATCH /incidents now updates the database record (was in-memory only, so
  status reverted on refresh and returned 404 after a restart). Resolving an
  incident resolves its linked events and recalculates vessel scores.
- Incident IDs continue from the highest persisted ID; the engine is
  rehydrated from the DB on startup, so a restart no longer reuses INC-0241
  and merges new events into an unrelated old incident.
- Vessel scores are recalculated from persisted open events on startup and
  written back (API showed stale baseline, then dropped to 0 on first tick).
- Simulation reset is non-destructive but closes all open events/incidents,
  so scores actually return to baseline.
- Correlation only evaluates rules containing the triggering event type, so
  an open network intrusion no longer shadows the physical-breach rule.
- navigation-anomaly / fire-emergency scenarios pointed at non-existent
  vessels ("meridian", "northstar"); now atlantic-trader / northern-star.
- New POST /api/v1/simulation/inject {vessel_id, event_type}. UI scenario
  buttons now inject the event they name for the selected target vessel
  (previously each button restarted a backend scenario at step 1 and ignored
  the vessel selector).
- /api/v1/simulation/next is async so its WebSocket broadcasts are delivered.
- Regression tests for all of the above (7 of 8 fail on the previous code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
